{"seq":5,"slug":"religious-studies","title":"宗教学","stage":"DONE","chapterCount":4,"docCount":11,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"宗教学\">宗教学</h1><p>我决定认真了解宗教，是从一个很具体的困惑开始的：为什么有人愿意为看不见、摸不着的东西改变整个人生？我身边有信佛的长辈、过圣诞节却不进教堂的朋友、还有把&quot;求神拜佛&quot;当成临时抱佛脚的同事。这些现象看起来零散，背后却共享一套人类共通的经验。宗教学（Religious Studies）正是把这套经验当成研究对象的学科。</p>\n<p>我想先澄清一个常见误会：宗教学不是&quot;传教学&quot;，也不是某个宗教的内部神学。它不预设任何一种信仰是真的，而是像研究语言、研究经济一样，把宗教当成一种可以观察、比较、分析的人类现象。学者可以是信徒，也可以是无神论者，但在研究时都要暂时&quot;悬置&quot;自己的信仰立场，去理解信徒眼中的世界为什么如此真实。</p>\n<p>这门学科有意思的地方在于它天然是跨学科的。要理解宗教，你会用到历史学的文献考证、人类学的田野观察、社会学的统计调查、心理学的体验分析，还有哲学对&quot;神圣&quot;&quot;超越&quot;这些概念的追问。所以学宗教学，某种意义上是在练习一种综合的眼光。</p>\n<p>这个知识库分四章。第一章讲理论与方法，回答&quot;宗教到底是什么&quot;&quot;我们用什么工具研究它&quot;这两个根本问题，这是后面所有内容的地基。第二章带你快速走一遍世界主要宗教——亚伯拉罕系（犹太教、基督教、伊斯兰教）、印度系（印度教、佛教、耆那教、锡克教）、东亚传统，目标不是背教义，而是建立一张&quot;地图&quot;。</p>\n<p>第三章把视角拉到社会层面，讨论宗教与现代化、世俗化、政治、性别的复杂关系，这些是当代最有争议也最现实的话题。第四章专门讲中国宗教，因为中国人的宗教生活有它独特的逻辑：不太讲究排他的&quot;皈依&quot;，更像是一种可以叠加、可以实用的信仰生态，理解它需要换一套框架。</p>\n<p>我写这个知识库时的定位，是一个零基础但好奇心很强的自学者。我尽量不堆术语，遇到必须用的概念会先用大白话讲清楚再给出学术名。每篇文末都有思考题和延伸阅读，方便你把读到的东西和自己的生活经验对照起来。</p>\n<p>如果你也曾经站在一座寺庙、教堂或清真寺门口，感到既陌生又好奇，那这个知识库就是为你准备的。我们不急着下结论，先学会观察和提问。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"theories-and-methods","title":"宗教学理论与方法","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/theories-and-methods","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-religious-studies","title":"什么是宗教学","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/theories-and-methods/what-is-religious-studies"},{"seq":2,"slug":"theories-of-religion","title":"解释宗教的主要理论","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/theories-and-methods/theories-of-religion"},{"seq":3,"slug":"methods-of-study","title":"宗教学的研究方法","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/theories-and-methods/methods-of-study"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"world-religions","title":"世界主要宗教","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/world-religions","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"abrahamic-religions","title":"亚伯拉罕系宗教：犹太教、基督教、伊斯兰教","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/world-religions/abrahamic-religions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"indian-religions","title":"印度系宗教：印度教、佛教、耆那教、锡克教","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/world-religions/indian-religions"},{"seq":3,"slug":"east-asian-traditions","title":"东亚宗教传统：儒、道与东亚佛教","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/world-religions/east-asian-traditions"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"religion-culture-society","title":"宗教与文化社会","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/religion-culture-society","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"religion-and-society","title":"宗教与社会：黏合剂还是分裂线","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/religion-culture-society/religion-and-society"},{"seq":2,"slug":"religion-and-modernity","title":"宗教与现代性：世俗化预言为何落空","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/religion-culture-society/religion-and-modernity"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"chinese-religions","title":"中国宗教","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/chinese-religions","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"chinese-folk-and-confucian","title":"民间信仰与儒家传统","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/chinese-religions/chinese-folk-and-confucian"},{"seq":2,"slug":"chinese-buddhism-and-daoism","title":"中国佛教与道教","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/chinese-religions/chinese-buddhism-and-daoism"},{"seq":3,"slug":"religion-in-contemporary-china","title":"当代中国宗教","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/philosophy/religious-studies/chinese-religions/religion-in-contemporary-china"}]}]}